4. Functional Flow
4.1 Journal Creation (Maker)
 * User navigates to Journal Posting.
 * System fetches the current-posting-date.
 * User enters Common Remarks and adds transaction rows.
 * User clicks Submit.
 * Validation: Client-side logic groups rows by Branch + Currency. It calculates Total Debit and Total Credit.
   * If totals do not match: Error Snackbar is shown.
   * If totals match: API payload is constructed.
 * Backend: JournalRequestService generates a Batch ID and saves data to JOURNAL_REQUEST table with status PENDING.
 * Notification: A system notification is generated for the "Authorizer" role.
4.2 Journal Authorization (Checker)
 * User navigates to Journal Authorization.
 * System fetches all requests where status = PENDING AND creatorId != currentUserId.
 * Bulk Action: User clicks "Accept" on the grid row.
   * System updates status to ACCEPTED.
   * System inserts records into GL_TRANSACTIONS table.
 * Partial Action: User opens "View Details", selects specific journals, and clicks "Reject Selected".
   * System updates status to REJECTED for those specific entries.
   * No GL entries are created for rejected items.
 * Notification: The original creator receives a notification regarding the decision.
4.3 Cancellation (Maker)
 * User navigates to Journal Status.
 * User identifies a PENDING batch they made a mistake on.
 * User clicks the Delete (Trash) icon.
 * System confirms the action and performs a hard delete of the request.
5. Error Handling
| Error Condition | Message Displayed |
|---|---|
| Debit/Credit Mismatch | "Submission failed. Totals for branch [Name] and currency [Code] do not match." |
| Missing Rows | "Branch [Name] must have at least one Debit and one Credit entry." |
| Duplicate CGL | "Duplicate CGL entry: [CGL] is used more than once for branch..." |
| Self-Approval Attempt | "You cannot approve or reject your own request." (Button Disabled or API Error). |
| Rejection without Remarks | "Approver remarks are required for rejection." |
| Invalid Amount Format | Field prevents entry of non-numeric characters or >4 decimal places. |
6. Security Requirements
 * Authentication: All API calls require a valid JWT Token in the header.
 * Authorization:
   * Only users with JOURNAL_MAKER permission can access the Posting screen.
   * Only users with JOURNAL_CHECKER permission can access the Authorization screen.
 * Segregation of Duties: The backend JournalRequestService enforces that executorId cannot equal creatorId for the same request role.
 * Data Integrity: Amounts are processed as BigDecimal in Java and BigInt (or stringified) in Frontend to prevent floating-point precision errors.
7. Acceptance Criteria
 * Users must be able to create a balanced batch across multiple branches and currencies in a single submission.
 * The system must generate a unique Batch ID and sequential Journal IDs (e.g., PREFIX-001, PREFIX-002) for every row.
 * Checkers must see all pending requests except those they created themselves.
 * Upon "Accept", data must be written to the GL_TRANSACTIONS table.
 * Upon "Reject", no data enters the GL; the status remains in JOURNAL_REQUEST as history.
 * Makers must be able to cancel requests only while they are in PENDING status.
